  "baseRefOid": "3095e3f294bf65f5e65c6ba6dd2b21984abe5864",
  "body": "Gather directly into the compressor/vision output buffers with one TileLang layout/unpadding/store kernel. Tail copies preserve opaque aligned words, rank-one results stay views, and tiny tails map a warp directly to each rank/row. Explicit geometry and disjoint-output checks replace the ATen layout-copy path.\n\nThe final composed source passes 1,266 correctness tests on both boots. All 24 main fused-gather GPU cases pass the zero-margin, five-standard-error gate on both boots. Larger-tail programs also qualify. Two tiny-tail event-based cases remain unresolved: event intervals are about 4 us around ~1 us kernels. Direct paired CUPTI kernel-duration checks are pending; the earlier results are retained. This PR stays in draft for those checks and the full-model inventory.\n\nFresh application of the independent series reproduces its recorded source tree; gather factories, wrappers, constants and non-shared files match the tested combination exactly. Doctor and diff checks pass. Actual NIC traffic and distributed serving remain release gates because the original dim-zero gather changes transport dispatch. No promoted recipe or serving process changes. See `experiments/2026-11-05-gather-tail-performance`.\n",
